Subject: [PATCH 170/174] docs: rebase the film grain onto the merged main line
 - spec status, the scene-referred gate, cinecam naming

The scene-referred pipeline became the main line on 2026-09-10 (dev fast-forwarded to
scene@a4fed24b, S9 editor CineCam preview and S10 CineCam Grade included), so the three
stage commits that were written against the stock dev@28a492c1 now sit on top of it. What
the move actually changes, and the repairs the rebase needed:

- FilmGrainSpec.md Status: the base is dev@a4fed24b and the scene-referred tree is no
  longer a tree to be "rebased off" - it is where we are.
- FilmGrainSpec.md section 2: the D9 scene-referred gate is back, and it zeroes the stock
  overlay grain on its own, independently of Grain_User_Active. The resolved line in
  DoFinalComposition is (bSceneReferred || bCineGrain) ? 0 : max(param, environment), so
  under Scene Referred the stock grain is already gone whether or not a cinecam is driving
  and our block takes the vacated slot - which is the "comes back as a sensor effect in S7"
  that the D9 comment promised, landing in the composition pass for now.
- FilmGrainSpec.md section 5.3: the capture-frame counter is stepped from
  ApplyGameOnlyEffects(), which since S9 is the ONE activation path for every effect - game
  mode from FinalizeGameCamera, the editor from the plugin's per-frame resolver when the
  viewport looks through a cinecam entity. So the grain follows the S9 editor policy for
  free, exactly like DOF and halation, with no second path to keep in step.
- Naming: the spec's prose says cinecam, per the 2026-09-09 rule. No identifier, cvar or
  post-effect param name changed.
- Two conflict-resolution artifacts repaired: PostProcess.cpp's file banner (a run of '='
  in the header was eaten by the resolution) and two lost blank lines / one lost line break
  in docs/ConsoleReference.md.

